ion you disclose to us.\n\nDo we process any sensitive personal information? Some of the information may be considered \"special\" or \"sensitive\" in certain jurisdictions, for example your racial or ethnic origins, sexual orientation, and religious beliefs. We do not request racial or ethnic origin, religious beliefs, or sexual-orientation information as account fields. Authentication credentials and information that users choose to include in public content still require protection; do not publish sensitive information about yourself or others.\n\nDo we collect any information from third parties? Optional social sign-in and Google Calendar connections provide authentication or connection information. We do not obtain user information from data brokers, public databases, or marketing partners for marketing.\n\nHow do we process your information? We process your information to provide, improve, and administer our Services, communicate with you, for security and fraud prevention, and to comply with law. We may also process your information for other purposes with your consent. We process your information only when we have a valid legal reason to do so. Learn more about how we process your information.\n\nIn what situations and with which parties do we share personal information? We may share information in specific situations and with specific third parties. Learn more about when and with whom we share your personal information.\n\nHow do we keep your information safe? We have adequate organizational and technical processes and procedures in place to protect your personal information. However, no electronic transmission over the internet or information storage technology can be guaranteed to be 100% secure, so we cannot promise or guarantee that hackers, cybercriminals, or other unauthorized third parties will not be able to defeat our security and improperly collect, access, steal, or modify your information. Learn more about how we keep your information safe.\n\nWhat are your rights? Depending on where you are located geographically, the applicable privacy law may mean you have certain rights regarding your personal information. Learn more about your privacy rights.\n\nHow do you exercise your rights? Contact support@1touch.football to request access, correction, deletion, or another applicable privacy right. We will consider and act upon any request in accordance with applicable data protection laws.\n\nWant to learn more about what we do with any information we collect? Review the Privacy Notice in full."
