          "Account information. Email registration uses an email address, username, nickname, and password. We store a password hash rather than the original password. We also process verification challenges, hashed verification codes, login-session token hashes, and expiry times. Optional social sign-in uses the provider and provider-issued account identifier, as explained below.\n\nCommunity and points. We process profile photographs, posts, comments, live-match chat messages, uploaded images or videos, reports, blocks, favorites, followed teams and players, likes, match-prediction selections, points committed to predictions, results, balances, and points history. We also store the country code provided by the device's region setting for the daily community-points period. This setting is not proof of nationality, residence, or physical location. Published profile and community information can be visible to others.\n\nOptional connections and notifications. Google Calendar connections use a Google account identifier, encrypted refresh token, app-created calendar identifier, and team subscriptions. Push delivery uses a generated installation identifier, FCM token, platform, locale, notification preferences, and delivery records. In-app notification records include relevant activity and read status.\n\nSupport and moderation. If you contact us, we process the contact details and information you include. Reports include the reported content reference, reason, reporter account reference, and moderation outcome. Please avoid sending information that is unnecessary for resolving your request.\n\nDevice access. The app requests access to the photo/video library for media selection and permission to display notifications. Google Calendar access is granted through Google authorization and is limited to calendars created by the app. The app does not request access to the device address book or precise GPS location. Device region settings also help choose sign-in suggestions on the device.\n\nNetwork and technical data. Our API receives IP addresses and request information, such as the requested route, time, and response status. Security rate limiting uses hashed request scopes. This is separate from Google's Mobile Ads SDK, which may process IP addresses, approximate location inferred from IP addresses, device identifiers, advertising interactions, and diagnostic information. We do not claim that non-personalized ads involve no personal information. See the advertising section below.\n\nSensitive information. Account login information combined with access credentials may be treated as sensitive personal information under California law. We use credentials for authentication and account security. We do not ask for race, religion, health information, or sexual orientation in account fields. Public posts and uploaded media can contain information chosen by their authors; do not publish sensitive information about yourself or others.\n\nGoogle API data. Our use of information received from Google APIs will adhere to the Google API Services User Data Policy (https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy), including its Limited Use requirements."
