cies.google.com/privacy) · Firebase privacy information (https://firebase.google.com/support/privacy)\nInformation and timing: Advertising identifiers, IP and interaction/diagnostic information when ads are requested; installation identifiers, push tokens and delivery data for messaging. See section 19.\nLocation information: International processing, including the United States. FCM runs on global infrastructure and has no country selection in our app. Google describes potential facilities in its data center list (https://www.google.com/about/datacenters/locations/) and Cloud locations (https://cloud.google.com/about/locations). We do not represent those lists as this device's actual processing location.\n\nRecipient and purpose: Porkbun LLC: support mailbox\nProvider privacy information (https://porkbun.com/legal/agreement/privacy_policy) · privacy@porkbun.com\nInformation and timing: Your sender address, message, attachments, and correspondence metadata when you email support@1touch.football.\nLocation information: Porkbun is a US provider and describes US and international processing. Our mail connection endpoints are in the US; this does not establish every mailbox, backup, or support-access country. A complete hosted-mail country list has not been made available to us.\n\nRecipient and purpose: Google, Apple, Kakao, and LINE: optional sign-in; Google Calendar: optional calendar connection\nInformation and timing: Authentication tokens and provider identifiers to verify a connection you select; calendar connection and match-event data if enabled. Provider account activity is also handled under that provider's notice.\nLocation information: Processing depends on the provider and account. See Google (https://policies.google.com/privacy), Apple (https://www.apple.com/legal/privacy/), Kakao (https://www.kakao.com/policy/privacy), and LINE (https://terms.line.me/line_rules/). We do not claim that choosing a sign-in provider confines processing to a particular country.\n\nCountries can have different privacy protections. Cloudflare and Firebase publish data processing terms that include international-transfer provisions; the safeguards that apply depend on the service and the particular transfer. Contact us for information about a transfer, applicable safeguards, or your rights.\n\nYou can decline optional social sign-in, calendar connection, notifications, or media uploads, or change available advertising choices. The corresponding optional feature may then be unavailable. Email registration remains a separate sign-in option. Account hosting is necessary to provide an account; you can stop using the service or request deletion. Accepting the Terms of Service is not blanket consent to international transfers or advertising processing. We will seek separate consent when the applicable law requires it."
